  "answers": [
    "Nothing has been deleted yet. This is what the command will do if you confirm:\n\n1. It removes the Google sign-in tokens stored on this computer.\n2. It cancels any Google import or sync jobs that are still running.\n3. It permanently deletes the Google records stored locally, along with the raw API responses kept with them.\n\nWhat it leaves alone:\n- **Your Takeout copy:** the Google Takeout data stays, because I set the Takeout option to off.\n- **Google's authorization:** I'm not revoking the app's access on Google's side, so it stays in place.\n\nThe deletion can't be undone. You could re-import the data later, but only while the app's authorization still works or from a Takeout file.\n\nThe confirmation code expires in about 5 minutes. Do you want me to go ahead? If it has expired by the time you reply, I'll request a new one.",
    "The first confirmation code expired before it was used, so nothing was deleted. I requested a new preview, and its actions are the same as before:\n\n1. Remove the Google sign-in tokens stored on this computer.\n2. Cancel any Google import or sync jobs that are still running.\n3. Permanently delete the local Google records and the raw API responses kept with them.\n\nYour Takeout copy stays, and Google's authorization stays in place. The deletion can't be undone.\n\nThe new code works for about 5 minutes, and your earlier approval doesn't carry over to it. Do you want me to go ahead with this one? Reply \"yes\" and I'll run it straight away."
